            <ArticleTitle>Mediastinal liposarcoma in a 30-year-old woman with dyspnea and chest pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>86-88</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.rmcr.2017.04.003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Mediastinal liposarcoma (ML) is a rare mesenchymal tumor, accounting for less than 1% of mediastinal tumors. They have a slow growth, so they may not give symptoms for a long time, until the tumor produces compression of close structures. The treatment of choice is surgery, which can be combined with chemo-radiotherapy. We present a case in which the diagnosis of a ML was made in a 30-year-old woman with dyspnea and chest pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
